ssti_thymeleaf_spel_sandbox -- reproduction log  (real-app-http REBUILD, 2026-07-15)
====================================================================================
CVE-2026-40478 (Thymeleaf restricted-SpEL sandbox: `new<TAB>Class` keyword-scanner bypass -> SSTI;
fixed 3.1.4.RELEASE) -> CVE-2026-41901 (incomplete fix: the 3.1.4 scanner is case-sensitive, so
UPPERCASE `NEW ` still escapes -- "improper recognition of unauthorized syntax patterns"; fixed
3.1.5.RELEASE). CWE-94 / CWE-917. Variant A (same restricted-SpEL sink, same read-exfil channel).

REBUILD NOTE: the previous build drove the library IN-PROCESS via `docker compose exec ... java Driver`
(BANNED). This rebuild runs the REAL published thymeleaf-spring6 inside a REAL Spring Boot 3 MVC web
app (embedded Tomcat) and triggers the SSTI over EXTERNAL HTTP. No in-process driver; no source-lift;
no Thymeleaf/Spring code modified.

Sink: user-controlled request parameter `expr` (GET/POST /render?expr=...) -> the controller inlines it
  into the RESTRICTED preprocessing position of a Thymeleaf view:  <div th:text="__${EXPR}__">x</div>
  -> StandardExpressionPreprocessor evaluates the inner expression under
     StandardExpressionExecutionContext.RESTRICTED -> SPELVariableExpressionEvaluator ->
     (getRestrictExternalAccess()) SpringStandardExpressionUtils.containsExternalAccess(EXPR)
     [+ ExpressionUtils.normalize] -> SpEL evaluation.
Canary (read-exfil): pcb.PcbFlagReader() reads /flag in its constructor; its toString() is inlined by
  preprocessing and rendered into the HTTP RESPONSE BODY. SUCCESS = flag token in the response body.
Roles: V0=thymeleaf-spring6 3.1.3.RELEASE (http://127.0.0.1:18413),
       V1=3.1.4.RELEASE (target, http://127.0.0.1:18414),
       V2=3.1.5.RELEASE (negative, http://127.0.0.1:18415).
Build: maven:3.9-eclipse-temurin-17 (-Dthymeleaf.version=${THYMELEAF_VER} overrides the Spring-Boot
  BOM); run: eclipse-temurin:17-jre; app = Spring Boot 3.3.5 (spring-boot-starter-web + -thymeleaf).

Source-verified guard evolution (tags thymeleaf-3.1.3/3.1.4/3.1.5.RELEASE; see patch.diff):
  * 3.1.3 normalize(): strips control chars -> `new<TAB>Class` collapses to `newClass` (no space
    after "new") -> scanner misses the keyword.
  * 3.1.4 normalize(): adds `|| Character.isWhitespace(c)` and appends a single space for whitespace
    -> `new<TAB>` becomes `new ` -> scanner detects "new " (CVE-2026-40478 fix). Still scans the
    LITERAL lowercase "new" (NEW_ARRAY="wen") without lowercasing the input -> UPPERCASE `NEW ` slips
    past, and SpEL parses `NEW` as the instantiation operator (case-insensitive).
  * 3.1.5 normalize(expression, true): lowercases the whole expression before scanning ->
    `NEW ` -> "new " -> detected (CVE-2026-41901 fix).

